      '<p>Step 1: A − λI = [[2 − λ, 1], [1, 2 − λ]].</p><p>Step 2: determinant (2 − λ)(2 − λ) − 1 × 1 = λ² − 4λ + 3 = (λ − 3)(λ − 1).</p><p>Step 3: roots λ = 3 and λ = 1.</p><p>Step 4: check A(1, 1) = (2 + 1, 1 + 2) = (3, 3) = 3 × (1, 1) and A(1, −1) = (2 − 1, 1 − 2) = (1, −1).</p><p>Quick checks: the eigenvalues add to the trace (2 + 2 = 4 = 3 + 1) and multiply to the determinant (4 − 1 = 3 = 3 × 1). Because A is symmetric, the eigenvectors are perpendicular, which is exactly what PCA relies on.</p>',
