      '<p>PCA works by finding the eigenvectors of the covariance matrix. Each eigenvector is a direction, and its eigenvalue is the variance of the data along that direction. Sorting by eigenvalue and keeping the top k gives the k directions that preserve the most spread. Always standardise features first, or a feature measured in large units (salary in rupees) will dominate one measured in small units (age in years).</p>',
