      '<p>Why ∂L/∂z = p − y: for y = 1, L = −log p, so ∂L/∂p = −1/p, and ∂p/∂z = p(1 − p). Multiply: −1/p × p(1 − p) = −(1 − p) = p − 1 = p − y.</p><p>Also ∂L/∂b = (p − y) × 1 ≈ −0.2689. With learning rate 0.5, w becomes 0.5 + 0.5 × 0.5379 ≈ 0.769.</p>',
