      '<p>Defaults are β = 0.9 for momentum, and β₁ = 0.9, β₂ = 0.999, ε = 10⁻⁸ for Adam. The bias correction matters early on: at step 1, m = 0.1 g, and dividing by 1 − 0.9 = 0.1 restores it to g. AdamW decouples weight decay from the adaptive step, and is the usual choice for training transformers.</p>',
