      '<p>For a twice differentiable function of one variable, convexity means f″(x) ≥ 0 everywhere. In many variables it means the Hessian has no negative eigenvalues. In practice, high dimensional networks are troubled more by saddle points than by bad local minima, and momentum and noise from mini batches help move past them.</p>',
